  "details": "By default when you create a particle system in Unity the max particles are automatically set to 1000, this is often unnecessary and can cause memory to be allocated where it doesn't need to be, along with dumping people's avatar performance.\n\nHaving a small warning when uploading an avatar with a default max particle value would likely help greatly, along with possibly adding an \"autofix\" button that automatically adjusts it to a more reasonable number.",
